    "explanation": "To both parties: this route-deviation claim cannot be finally decided on the present record, so it goes to a human reviewer and the disputed amount is held rather than collected or refunded. Here is why, and what would settle it.\n\nFirst, what the record does show. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00107) measures 17.57 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a platform optimal of 14.0 km — an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5%, clearing both limbs of POL-RD-01 (over 20% and over 0.8 km). The driver's own account, \"I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it,\" concedes he left the CTE corridor the optimal route uses. So a deviation is made out, and the driver's traffic explanation does not exonerate it: POL-RD-03 requires a traffic_advisory naming a road the optimal route uses, and the only such artifact, EV-ADVIS-00107-01, is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) — no advisory was issued for the CTE that evening. POL-RD-08 also puts the driver to a specific artifact, which a bare \"traffic was bad\" cannot supply.\n\nSecond, why no money can issue. The excess the ruling would rest on is measured by one artifact only, the GPS trace, and that artifact is down-weighted to 0.30. The admissibility pre-pass tagged EV-GPS-00107 IMPAIRED with codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED — a 331.8 m multipath jump between 21:44:52 and 21:45:02 on the final approach into Raffles Place, implying an impossible speed. Two separate things must be said about it: it is down-weighted for confidence to 0.30, but it is NOT impaired for policy under POL-RD-07 — there is no gap over 90 s (max gap 0.0 s), the 331.8 m jump is under the 500 m limb, and sampling is a steady 10 s, under the 30 s limb — so a deviation may still be established on it, and it is. The obstacle is weight, not usability. The trip record's actual_distance_km (17.6) and the fare breakdown's distance_charged_km (17.60) are not independent of the trace: POL-RD-01 calls the trip-record figure a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement, and POL-RD-07(ii) directs me to check whether a billed distance is such a copy — it is. The driver's admission corroborates the route and satisfies the extra corroboration the rider's profile requires under POL-RD-08 (5 claims in 60 days, 1 substantiated), but as a statement in case.dispute with no weight_multiplier it enters neither the minimum nor the maximum of the confidence cap. The cap is therefore the minimum weight of the artifacts carrying the deciding fact — 0.30 — and the bundle mean of about 0.76 is context only, not the cap. 0.30 is below the platform-wide floor of 0.70, so POL-RD-10(1) makes the escalation mandatory. A second trigger also fires: POL-RD-10(5), because an exculpatory clause (POL-RD-03) was invoked against an artifact that is missing from the pool.\n\nOn the remaining points: POL-RD-06 is not engaged — the deviation is not MATERIAL and the citable counters (deviation_flags_90d 1, completed_trips_90d 619) show no pattern — so no full refund and no driver-conduct referral arise. POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 do not apply (no rider instruction, no endpoint amendment, vehicle_type RYDE_X). Nothing is due on the pass-through lines under POL-RD-09: erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00, with no surcharge to correct. For completeness only, had confidence permitted a money ruling, POL-RD-02 would give recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 14.0 + 0.28 x 24.0) x 1.35) + 0.80 = 29.177; refund = 36.60 - 29.177 = 7.423, rounded up to SGD 7.45 — a PARTIAL_REFUND. That is not paid here, because escalation replaces the ruling.\n\nWhat would resolve it: an independent measurement of the trip's actual distance that is not a copy of this trace (for example a platform-derived distance from a second source, or a trace reacquired clear of the multipath outlier), and/or a traffic_advisory covering the CTE for the evening of 18 July 2026, which would let POL-RD-03 be run."
  },
