    "explanation": "Both of you should know why this goes to a human reviewer instead of being paid out or closed, and exactly what the record does and does not settle.\n\nWHAT IS ESTABLISHED. On the night of 18 July 2026 the trip ran Ang Mo Kio to One Raffles Place. The platform's route estimate (trip_record.optimal_distance_km) was 14.0 km. The GPS trace measures the drive at 17.57 km, an excess of 3.57 km, or 25.5% — over both POL-RD-01 thresholds (20% and 0.8 km). The driver's own account ('I went by Newton and Kim Seng to avoid it') confirms he left the CTE/optimal corridor, and his in-app reply offers only a jam excuse. So a route deviation is established (POL-RD-08's extra corroboration for a sub-30% claim is met by that admission, and waypoint_hint was null on both chat messages, so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04; no pin amendment under POL-RD-05; vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 is off). No exoneration is available: POL-RD-03 requires a traffic_advisory for the CTE that evening and none exists (EV-ADVIS-00107-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), and a bare 'it was jammed' cites no artifact and is discarded under POL-RD-08.\n\nWHY IT STILL CANNOT BE PAID. The 3.57 km rests on the GPS trace EV-GPS-00107 alone. That artifact is down-weighted to weight 0.30 with issue codes GPS_DRIFT and IMPLAUSIBLE_SPEED (a 331.8 m multipath jump at 21:44:57 implying 193.6/238.9 kph). It is NOT impaired for policy — gaps are empty (max_gap_sec 0.0), the jump is under the 500 m limb and sampling is a steady 10 s under the 30 s limb — so it can still establish the deviation, and POL-RD-10(3) does not fire. But under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence is capped by the weight of the artifact carrying the deciding fact, and nothing else independently carries the excess: trip_record.actual_distance_km 17.6 is a rounded convenience copy POL-RD-01 forbids citing for the threshold test, and fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km 17.60 is that same measurement re-published, so it lifts nothing (POL-RD-07's independence check). The driver's admission carries the route but a counterparty statement has no weight and enters neither the cap's minimum nor its maximum.\n\nTHE RULING. Confidence is therefore capped at 0.30, below the 0.70 platform floor, and POL-RD-10(1) makes escalation mandatory. The disputed SGD 36.60 is held — neither refunded nor treated as settled; no POL-RD-02 figure (which would have been a SGD 7.45 partial refund on the 36.60 charged) issues. Driver compensation is nil: the billed distance (17.60 km) is not less than the trace (17.57 km), so POL-RD-04's unbilled-kilometre head is not engaged. No referral arises: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 over 619 trips, so no POL-RD-06 pattern and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, and the fare carries no ERP lines and no surcharge, so POL-RD-09(4) produces no billing-integrity finding.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT: an independent measurement of the distance actually driven (a platform-derived figure not copied from the down-weighted trace), or a traffic advisory covering the CTE on the evening of 18 July 2026."
